# Line endings.
#
# This repository is written on Windows and run on Linux, so the checkout must not
# decide the line endings. With core.autocrlf=true — the default of the Git for
# Windows installer — a clone would otherwise get CRLF in every text file, and a
# shell script with CRLF line endings fails on the server with
#
#   deploy/scripts/demo_up.sh: line 2: $'\r': command not found
#
# Everything below keeps the file LF in the working tree as well as in the
# repository, on every platform.

# Normalise to LF in the repository for anything Git sees as text. Binary files are
# detected and left alone.
* text=auto

# Read by a Linux shell, a container entrypoint, or Docker.
*.sh        text eol=lf
run         text eol=lf
Dockerfile* text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
